+# Due Date for Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos bekommen ein optionales Fälligkeitsdatum (`dueDate`, `YYYY-MM-DD`), das in der API validiert wird und in der Liste mit „überfällig"-Markierung plus „nur überfällige"-Filter angezeigt wird.
+
+**Architecture:** Validierung und Speicherung von `dueDate` im bestehenden Store (`src/store.mjs`), Durchreichen über die bestehende JSON-API (`src/app.mjs`, keine neuen Routen), UI-Anpassungen in `public/index.html` (Datum neben Titel, Überfällig-Markierung, clientseitiger Filter). TDD: erst fehlschlagende Tests, dann minimale Implementierung.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24 builtins only (node:http, node:test), vanilla JS im Browser. Zero dependencies.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-15-due-date-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only (AGENTS.md).
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` and map to HTTP 400 (bestehender Mechanismus in `src/app.mjs`).
+- TDD: write a failing test in `test/` first, then implement.
+- Every UI element tests rely on carries a `data-testid` (existing: `todo-list`, `todo-item`, `todo-title`).
+- `dueDate` format: `YYYY-MM-DD`, strict calendar validation (reject 2026-02-30, 2026-13-01, 2026-1-5, etc.).
+- Removing a due date: PATCH with `dueDate: null`.
+- Overdue = `done === false` AND `dueDate` strictly before today (UTC date, no time). Todos without `dueDate` are never overdue.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` filters server-side with that definition; without the parameter the response is unchanged.
+- UI date display format: German `DD.MM.YYYY` (e.g. „20.10.2026").
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Invalid date strings that look almost right (`2026-1-5`, `20.10.2026`, `2026/10/20`, `2026-02-30`) must all yield HTTP 400 — pinned by tests in Task 1.
+- `dueDate: null` must remove the date, not store the string "null" — pinned in Task 2.
+- Overdue boundary: a todo due *today* is NOT overdue; due *yesterday* is — pinned in Task 2.
+- Overdue requires `done === false`: a done todo with a past date is NOT overdue — pinned in Task 2.
+- Todos without `dueDate` are never overdue — pinned in Task 2.
+- Existing todos without `dueDate` must keep working and return `dueDate: null` — pinned in Task 2 (existing test updated).
+- The overdue filter must not mutate or hide data permanently; toggling back shows all todos — exercised in the end-to-end test.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — dueDate validation helper and add/update support
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Modify: `test/store.test.mjs` (create)
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `isValidDueDate(value)` — internal helper in `src/store.mjs`, returns true only for `null` or a string matching a real calendar date in `YYYY-MM-DD`.
+- Produces: `store.add({ title, dueDate })` — accepts optional `dueDate`; throws `ValidationError('dueDate must be a valid YYYY-MM-DD date or null')` on invalid values; stored todo has `dueDate` (string or `null`).
+- Produces: `store.update(id, patch)` — accepts `dueDate` in patch with the same validation; `dueDate: null` clears the date.
+
